      <abstract>
        <para>
          A normal reboot runs the firmware initialization and the boot loader before the new
          kernel starts, which takes time, especially on servers. With &kexec;, you can skip both
          steps. This article explains when a &kexec; reboot is useful, when you still need a
          full reboot and how to reboot with &kexec; on &productname;.
        </para>
        <para><emphasis role="bold">Prerequisites</emphasis></para>
        <itemizedlist>
          <listitem>
            <para>
              The <package>kexec-tools</package> and <package>update-bootloader</package>
              packages, which are installed by default.
            </para>
          </listitem>
        </itemizedlist>
      </abstract>
